class.description:
[AudioDeviceSettingsServer] is the settings domain [code]"audio_device"[/code]: it stores the output and the input device of [AudioServer] ([member AudioServer.output_device], [member AudioServer.input_device]) for the player, loads them when the game starts and applies them in [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SERVERS], before the first sound plays. The settings resource is an [AudioDeviceSettings]. The file is [code]user://settings/audio_device.ini[/code] by default; as a single record it is never stored as CSV. The bus volumes are a separate domain, see [AudioBusSettingsServer].
Device names are the names of the active audio driver (see [method AudioServer.get_output_device_list]), so they only mean something on the same machine and with the same driver. A device that the driver does not list (unplugged, another machine or driver) is replaced by [code]"Default"[/code] when the value is set or loaded, with a verbose message only and no error. The file keeps the old name until it is saved again, so a headset that is plugged in again is used at the next start.
Device selection is supported by the WASAPI driver (Windows), PulseAudio and ALSA (Linux and *BSD) and CoreAudio on macOS. The XAudio2 driver, Android, iOS and the Web only have [code]"Default"[/code]; use [method SettingsServer.is_value_supported] or [method is_device_selection_supported] to hide the option there. The input device also needs [member ProjectSettings.audio/driver/enable_input].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	var output_list = $OutputList
	output_list.visible = AudioDeviceSettingsServer.is_value_supported(&"output_device")
	for device in AudioServer.get_output_device_list():
		output_list.add_item(device)
		if device == AudioDeviceSettingsServer.get_output_device():
			output_list.select(output_list.item_count - 1)

func _on_output_list_item_selected(index):
	AudioDeviceSettingsServer.set_output_device($OutputList.get_item_text(index))
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    var outputList = GetNode<OptionButton>("OutputList");
    // Methods of the base class are called through Singleton.
    outputList.Visible = AudioDeviceSettingsServer.Singleton.IsValueSupported("output_device");
    foreach (string device in AudioServer.GetOutputDeviceList())
    {
        outputList.AddItem(device);
        if (device == AudioDeviceSettingsServer.GetOutputDevice())
        {
            outputList.Select(outputList.ItemCount - 1);
        }
    }
}

private void OnOutputListItemSelected(long index)
{
    AudioDeviceSettingsServer.SetOutputDevice(GetNode<OptionButton>("OutputList").GetItemText((int)index));
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] In C#, the static class [code skip-lint]AudioDeviceSettingsServer[/code] only has the methods of this class. The methods of [SettingsServer] are called through [code]AudioDeviceSettingsServer.Singleton[/code].
[b]Note:[/b] Most drivers switch the device on their audio thread, so [member AudioServer.output_device] may report the old device for a short time after a change.
